  "body": "Due to regulatory, administrative and other reasons, there will be rooms or even whole homeservers with disabled E2E encryption. But that doesn't mean we should drop related security features like cryptographical identity and message signing.\n\nWe can reuse existing session key management mechanisms to provide security against homeserver/federation-side tampering and client session compromising, by conditionally switching AES-CBC with no-op.\n\nThis issue extends from #212",
